candle-audio-sheetsage2 — NOTICE
================================

This crate is a native Rust / Candle reimplementation of the SheetSage2 music-transcription model
and its MERT-v2-FullSong encoder, made for the SceneWorks inference workspace (epic sc-22988,
story sc-22996).

Upstream works
--------------

SheetSage2 and MERT2 (MERT-v2-FullSong) by Multimodal Art Projection (m-a-p).

  * m-a-p/SheetSage2
      https://huggingface.co/m-a-p/SheetSage2
      model weights pinned at revision eab522a8168e8b8b8c4856bf8609cd86198f01fe
      post-processing behaviour ported from revision 4f89269db831bdc1880124164a00d4f9385cd129
      (same weight file; key-aware chord spelling and canonical key labels)
  * m-a-p/MERT-v2-FullSong
      https://huggingface.co/m-a-p/MERT-v2-FullSong
      pinned at revision d8ba1c745e733b3908ce6ad16ebeb17ac7600a42

Licence terms published upstream
--------------------------------

Both repositories ship the same LICENSE file, titled "MERT2 model-weight license". It licenses
"the MERT2-30s and MERT2-FS checkpoint weights in model.safetensors" under Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ , and states that it "does not replace separately
applicable licenses for code or dependencies". Both model cards declare `license: cc-by-nc-4.0`;
the SheetSage2 card describes it as the licence of the weights.

That grant covers model weights only. The remote Python code published in the two repositories
(modeling_mert2.py, configuration_mert2.py, modeling_sheetsage2.py, generation_sheetsage2.py,
tokenization_sheetsage2.py, notation_sheetsage2.py, chord_spelling_sheetsage2.py,
exports_sheetsage2.py, midi_sheetsage2.py and the other *.py files) carries no licence header, no
SPDX tag and no code licence file: upstream grants NO licence for that code.

Status of this crate's code
---------------------------

This crate contains no upstream code verbatim; it was written in Rust from a reading of that
remote Python at the revisions above, closely enough that its outputs are byte-identical to
upstream's. It may nevertheless be a derivative of that code, for which no licence has been
granted. The crate's `license = "CC-BY-NC-4.0"` field is a PROVISIONAL disposition recorded by
sc-22989 (crates/audio/candle-audio-yue2/src/license.rs, CODE_TERMS / COVER_PORT): it keeps the
code at the most restrictive terms of the surrounding repositories until the owner records a basis
(an explicit code licence from Multimodal Art Projection, or an owner decision). It is not a
licence granted by the upstream authors. Until that decision the crate stays gated: it is not
composed into the audio catalog or any runtime bundle, and it is admitted to the workspace only by
one scoped cargo-deny exception (deny.toml).

Weights are never vendored here. The small safetensors files under testdata/tiny/ are seeded random
weights with the upstream architecture, generated by scripts/reference/sheetsage2/native_parity.py;
they contain no upstream weights.

Modifications relative to upstream
----------------------------------

  * Reimplemented in Rust on Candle; no Python, PyTorch, torchaudio or Transformers at runtime.
  * The mel front end reads its Hann window, filterbank and normalization statistics from the
    checkpoint and computes the STFT with a native radix-2 FFT.
  * Attention over the fixed 300 s window is computed in query chunks (same result, bounded memory).
  * The rank-64 LoRA adapters are merged into the MERT projections in float32 at load, as upstream
    does; no merged checkpoint is written or distributed.
  * MIDI files are written and read by a native Standard MIDI File implementation reproducing
    pretty_midi 0.2.10 / mido 1.3.3 byte for byte.
  * Chord spelling follows the head revision 4f89269 rather than the release eab522a.
  * Added, not in upstream: a persisted, integrity-checked and replayable review artifact; an
    explicit refusal of transcriptions with no melody (upstream returns a rest-only score); octave,
    harmony-collapse, voice-assignment and sparse-melody warnings; unload accounting; and the YuE2
    cover-request path.

Attribution for the weights, as the upstream LICENSE requests: MERT2 (MERT-v2-FullSong),
https://huggingface.co/m-a-p/MERT-v2-FullSong; SheetSage2, https://huggingface.co/m-a-p/SheetSage2.
